        {
          "name": "Struct Name",
          "type": "StructName* ) -> decltype ( sizeof ("
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<StructName> auto",
      "docs": "This function should be called in the following way to take advantage of SFINAE and perform compile-time\nerror checking for declared types:\nstatic_assert(IsDeclaredType((struct MyStruct*)Ptr), \"Error message..\");\nIf MyStruct is not declared, the cast will pass a void* pointer to IsDeclaredType(). Otherwise, if MyStruct\nis declared then the cast will pass a MyStruct* pointer to IsDeclaredType()."
